But, I also said [last month](2026-june) that I wanted to try and listen to 3 full albums
a week just sitting and enjoying. I didn't manage to do a full 3 every week, but I did
listen to a few and wrote a small 1-2 sentence blurb for each:
* [Rem - Vincent's Tale](https://renmakesmusic.bandcamp.com/album/vincents-tale-2):
  Surprisingly heartfelt white boy beats.
* [Rozwell Kid - Precious Art](https://rozwellkid.bandcamp.com/album/precious-art): I
  mostly bought this because of the saguaro on the cover. Not the peak of lyricism, but
  some killer riffs.
* [Darren Korb - Songs of Supergiant Games](https://supergiantgames.bandcamp.com/album/songs-of-supergiant-games): Tour de
  force of the best in the business. Gives me goosebumps every time.
* [Phantom Spell - Heather & Hearth](https://phantomspell.bandcamp.com/album/heather-hearth): "When one day I pass beyond,
  gift my bones back to the sand. Sow my soul, keep me well, and let my heart beat with
  the land." Big reason I finished [The Cliffside](https://purpleshirt.dev/writing/the-cliffside/).
* [King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard - Butterfly 3000](https://kinggizzard.bandcamp.com/album/butterfly-3000): I really feel
  like this one would be higher on my KGLW ranking if I took a lot of drugs, but I don't.
  Still lovely.

## Watched

A rare "Watched" appearance! I also said last month that I wanted to watch one new movie a
week. Out of a possible 5 weeks, I only did 3 movies, but that's OK with me. In order:
* [Boogie Nights](https://letterboxd.com/film/boogie-nights/): I knew nothing about this
  going in other than that a lot of people say that it's outstanding. Can confirm, it is
  absolutely outstanding. Every character is super developed for being such a giant
  ensemble cast. Only good Mark Wahlberg performance in existence.
* [Zoolander](https://letterboxd.com/film/zoolander/): I somehow managed to make it my
  entire life without seeing Zoolander. A couple jokes have not aged particularly well,
  but overall absolutely killer hour and a half of one liners. Ya-goggly.
* [Avatar Aang](https://letterboxd.com/film/avatar-aang-the-last-airbender/): All of the
  money went into the bending. Which, granted, the bending looks absolutely sick as fuck.
  Sadly, it has also been the final nail in the coffin for me of the ATLA franchise,
  wherein I will now refuse to watch anything but the original show and Legend of Korra in
  order to preserve how good they are. Story and dialogue in this movie was so predictable
  that I could feel myself going full monkey brain until Toph threw some rocks around
  again and I could enjoy what was on screen.

## Made

* My biggest project this month was [reviving an old MacBook Pro](macbook-revive-part-1)
  to turn it into a dedicated dev machine. That process was both fun and satisfying, and
  I've got a great little machine now to start plugging away at software things.
* I did also do a fair bit more cooking this month, which was great. Particular highlights
  were Pasta Arrabiatta (simple, but a variant I had not made before), and a
  chipotle-pepper soup that turned out excellent.

# Stuff I Only Sorta Did or Didn't Do

* My running again suffered this month (partially self-imposed from playing too much beach
  volleyball, partially due to lingering knee pain). I really need to kick myself into gear
  next month if I still want to feel comfortable going into the marathon I'm running in
  October.
* I also didn't practice guitar as much as I intended, *but I did practice*, which was a
  big step up from last month. So aiming to keep that up.

# Stuff I'm Gonna Do in August
I want to keep up my trend of watching new films and enjoying music just to enjoy, and as
part of that my real major overlying "thing" for June is a digital decluttering. I've been
reading [Digital Minimalism](https://hardcover.app/books/digital-minimalism) (begrudgingly
at first, and then it actually turned out to be pretty solid, even if lots of the stuff it
points out is already obvious), and would like to actively try a decluttering as
recommended this month. There's a few reasons for August in particular:
* Barring extremely shit weather, I'm spending the first few days of it doing a multi-day
  backpacking trip alone. This presents a guaranteed set of time where I won't be on my
  phone anyway, with the extra punch of "walking through forest for my mental health."
* Even though I haven't had any social media accounts for 5+ years at this point (minus
  strava, which only really half-counts), I have had a lot of mood swings this year
  related to stuff to do with the digital realm. So trying to regain some of that offline
  focus would be good.
* I've already rediscovered a few old hobbies and signed up to try out a couple new ones
  anyway that all begin or continue into this month (all of which are non-digital), so yet
  more opportunity to leave my phone at home.
* Weirdly, I want to rediscover my love for video games as an art form. I've not spent
  time playing games recently both because I'm busy, but also because my screen time is a
  lot of passive consumption (blogs, some livestreams, some youtube, etc). I'd like to
  turn it back into enjoying some active engagement with the art (and this is the same
  reason for watching good movies and listening to good albums without having them be
  simple "background noise").

Anyway, we'll see how it goes! If my hiking trip gets rained out, I'll be spending that
time running in one of the nature reserves near Amsterdam where possible, or doing some
other outdoors-y substitute. Here's to no more heat waves!
